3) N+/PW, P+/NW & NW/PSUB junction diode

 A) HSPICE LEVEL 49 :

    ## library files:

    All models are included in file 'log018_1.l' for H97.2
                               and  'log018_2.l' for H98.2
      .lib DIO

        Scalable junction diode model ( level 3 ) was used for modeling.
        User can change the AREA, PJ (perimeter) according their layout
        to simulate their circuit.


4) INTERCONNECTION MODEL TABLE in intercon directory

       1. typ_strA : typical case, structure A interconnection table

       2. typ_strB : typical case, structure B interconnection table

       3. wor_strA : worst   case, structure A interconnection table

       4. wor_strB : worst   case, structure B interconnection table

       5. bes_strA : best    case, structure A interconnection table

       6. bes_strB : best    case, structure B interconnection table


5) RESISTOR Equivalent Circuit Model

      resmodel.spi

              Resistor Type             Best      Typical    Worst
         ------------------------------------------------------------- 
           N+ Diff. w/i Silicide        rn_b       rn_t       rn_w
           P+ Diff. w/i Silicide        rp_b       rp_t       rp_w
           N+ Diff. w/o Silicide       rnrpo_b    rnrpo_t    rnrpo_w
           P+ Diff. w/o Silicide       rprpo_b    rprpo_t    rprpo_w
           N-well ( under OD )         rnwod_b    rnwod_t    rnwod_w
         -------------------------------------------------------------
        
       User must include ResModel.spi file and call Lib DIO  when use these 
       Resistor equivalent circuit models. The method of using these models
       is the same as subcircuit. 

       If the simulated subcircuit uses small width, i.e., <2um, in N+ diff 
       and P+ diff w/i silicide, the resistor equivalent circuit model
       is:

              Resistor Type             Best      Typical    Worst
         ------------------------------------------------------------- 
           N+ Diff. w/i Silicide        rns_b      rns_t      rns_w
           P+ Diff. w/i Silicide        rps_b      rps_t      rps_w


