7) RAW DATA :

      ## raw data files:

        1.  readme.txt : explain how to read the raw data format 

        2.  nmos.log   : for 1.8V NMOS DEVICES GROUP 

        3.  pmos.log   : for 1.8V PMOS DEVICES GROUP

        4.  nanmos.log : for 1.8V native NMOS DEVICES GROUP

        5.  nmos3v.log : for 3.3V NMOS DEVICES GROUP

        6.  pmos3v.log : for 3.3V PMOS DEVICES GROUP

        7.  nanmos3v.log  : for 3.3V native NMOS DEVICES GROUP

8) GDS file

   'a24.gds.Z.uuencode'

   The GDS file of 0.18um bipolar layout for the 0.18um bipolar model.
   It is a uuencoded and compressed file.

9) layer.txt

   CAD layer definition for the 0.18um bipolar layout GDS file. 

10) UPDATE HISTORY :

        V1.5 : 1. Update 0.18um 1.8V native NMOS model from V0.1 to V1.1.
               2. Create 0.18um 3.3V native NMOS model V1.1.
               3. Update resistance models: change resistance table format;
                  update Rs data for poly, diffusion and well; add effective
                  width range definition for Rs in poly, diffusion, and well;
                  and update VC1 and VC2 with different applied voltage for
                  different patterns.
               4. Add resistor equivalent circuit model in floppy.
               5. Update 10x10, 5x5, 2x2 bipolar models for HSPICE and SPECTRE
                  compatible.
               6. Correct typing error in section 8.3 comparison tables: 1.8V
                  PMOS 10/0.18 simulated Vt data in FS corner; 3.3V PMOS 10/0.3
                  simulated Vt data in SS, FF, SF, and FS corner; and 3.3V PMOS
                  10/0.3 simulated data in SF and FS corner.
               7. Remove HSPICE 97.4 and SPECTRE 4.4.1 (replaced by 4.4.3) from
                  model cards.
        V1.4 : 1. Create 0.18um 1.8V native NMOS preliminary model.
               2. Add three HSPICE level 3 noise parameters for both 1.8V 
                  and 3.3V normal N/PMOS models in HSPICE model files. 
               3. Change HDIF value to TSMC minimum rule in both 1.8V and 3.3V
                  N/PMOS model.
               4. Update simulation result of ring-oscillator speed by using
                  H98.2 in section 3.4.
               5. Update worst-case simulated results of ring-oscillator speed
                  by using H98.2 and setting HDIF=0.2um, TSMC minimum rule
                  (section 8.4).

        V1.3:  1. Modify the parameters, VTH0, LVTH0, WVTH0, PVTH0, AGS, LAGS,
                  WAGS and PAGS in the pch3.3/pch3_3 of 3.3V PMOS model to fix
                  the continuity issues at model boundary.
               2. Add 3.3V NMOS with ESD implant models.
               3. Update interconnect capacitance models.
               4. Update sheet resistance, TC1, TC2, and deltaW of metal1~6 in
                  resistor table.
               5. Add the P-substrate voltage coefficients of NW diffusion 
                  (under OD) resistance in resistor table.

	V1.2 : 1. Added 5-corners 3.3V mos models. 

	V1.1 : 1. Updated 5-corners 1.8V mos models. 
 	       2. Updated 10x10 bipolar model.
	       3. Added 5x5 and 2x2 bipolar models. 
               4. Updated diode models.
 	       5. Update interconnect capacitance models.
   	       6. Added resistance models.
 	       7. Delete 3.3V mos model(will be included in V1.2 release).

      	V0.2 : 1. Add 1.8V model corner, 3.3V MOS model & corner.

      	V0.1 : 1. Create preliminary model.
